# rinsai opening set, v2 — frozen.
#
# One USI `position` argument per line (`startpos moves …`); `#` starts a
# comment and blank lines are ignored — the same conventions as
# bench-v1.sfen. The SPRT harness plays every line twice per pair, colours
# swapped (CLAUDE.md §3).
#
# ⚠️ FROZEN. Paired-game results are comparable only within one opening set,
# so a later set is a new file, openings-v3.sfen, never an edit to this one.
#
# PROVENANCE (CLAUDE.md §2). floodgate game records are factual data
# (DESIGN.md §7); the game behind each line is named on the comment above
# it. Generated by `cargo run --release -p xtask -- gen-openings` at rev
# fixture, splitmix64 seed 0x52494e5341492d31.
#   source days: 2026-06-01 2026-06-02 — 11 records, 7 qualifying games,
#     7 replayed clean, 2 rejected on rate,
#     1 on termination, 1 on length, 0 on replay
#   game filter: both floodgate rates >= 3000, ends %TORYO or %KACHI,
#     >= 60 plies, every replayed move legal
#   window: plies 12..=24, side to move not in check —
#     88 snapshots, 81 unique positions
#   pick and balance, one lazily-evaluated pass: candidates visited in
#     seeded Fisher-Yates order, the per-game cap (<= 2 of one
#     source game; 0 skipped over it) checked before any search;
#     5 searched at depth 3 capped at 2000000 nodes,
#     16 MiB table; 1 fell outside ±100 cp or carried a
#     mate score; the first 4 survivors are the set, emitted in
#     (day, file, ply) order.
#   eval= on each comment line is rinsai's own score, from the side to move,
#     and d= is the depth it came from: the deepest iteration that searched
#     *every* root move. A search the node cap interrupts is judged on the
#     last iteration that finished, never on the partial one — whose score
#     is the best over a prefix of the root list and so a lower bound. That
#     is the one thing v2 changed from v1, which read the partial line.
# Regeneration from the same cached inputs, rev and seed is byte-identical
# (`--rev` replays the rev recorded above, since HEAD moves when the file
# is committed); crates/xtask/tests/gen_openings_fixture.rs is the
# executable form of that claim, at fixture scale.

# 2026-06-01/wdoor+floodgate-300-10F+62KIN_Suisho11_4c+Allihn_Condenser+20260601130001.csa ply=23 eval=+15 d=3
startpos moves 4i5h 8c8d 5h4h 8d8e 6i7h 8e8f 8g8f 8b8f P*8g 8f8b 2g2f 3c3d 2f2e 2b3c 4g4f 7a6b 3i3h 6c6d 3h4g 6b6c 3g3f 4a3b 2i3g
# 2026-06-01/wdoor+floodgate-300-10F+62KIN_Suisho11_4c+clomeprop+20260601143005.csa ply=12 eval=+0 d=3
startpos moves 4i5h 3c3d 5h4h 1c1d 6i7h 8c8d 2g2f 8d8e 2f2e 2b3c 7g7f 3a2b
# 2026-06-01/wdoor+floodgate-300-10F+62KIN_Suisho11_4c+jhbr2+20260601113000.csa ply=23 eval=+0 d=3
startpos moves 4i5h 8c8d 5h4h 8d8e 6i7h 3c3d 2g2f 4a3b 2f2e 2b3c 7g7f 3a2b 8h7g 3c7g 7h7g 2b3c 4g4f 7a6b 3g3f 7c7d 3i3h 8a7c 6g6f
# 2026-06-02/wdoor+floodgate-300-10F+62KIN_Suisho11_4c+Allihn_Condenser+20260602050002.csa ply=21 eval=+15 d=3
startpos moves 4i5h 8c8d 5h4h 8d8e 6i7h 8e8f 8g8f 8b8f P*8g 8f8b 2g2f 3c3d 2f2e 2b3c 4g4f 7a7b 3i3h 4a3b 3g3f 6c6d 3h4g
